# Copied to .env by `make seed` (or `make up`) when .env does not exist yet; an existing .env is
# never overwritten, so a key added here later must be added to your .env by hand — `make doctor`
# names any that are missing. Never commit .env.
#
# TWO HALVES:
#   1. THE PLATFORM'S SECRETS (this first section): every line is REQUIRED and SET. Docker Compose
#      reads them (`--env-file .env`), and so do the control plane's start block, the test harness
#      and several scripts. Change the `change-me-locally` values before anything leaves a laptop.
#   2. THE CONTROL PLANE'S SETTINGS (below): every line is COMMENTED OUT, showing its default.
#      Uncomment a line to change it.
#
# ───────────────────────────────────── 1. THE PLATFORM'S SECRETS ─────────────────────────────────────
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me-locally
LITELLM_MASTER_KEY=sk-manifest-local-master
LITELLM_SALT_KEY=sk-manifest-local-salt
# Host Node processes (control plane, admin UI, console) ignore the macOS
# keychain, so they need this explicitly — S7 §Evidence 7.
NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=./infra/ca/manifest-root.crt
SSP_SECRET_SALT=change-me-locally
SSP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-locally
# SimpleSAMLphp reads its SP metadata as this SELECT-only role (§9). Created by
# infra/lib/ensure-idp-sql.sh on every `make up`.
SSP_RO_PASSWORD=change-me-locally
# The control plane connects as `manifest_app`, NOT as `manifest`. `manifest` is
# POSTGRES_USER and therefore a superuser, and a superuser bypasses every
# privilege check — which makes §20's append-only events grant unimplementable.
# Created by infra/lib/ensure-app-role.sh on every `make up`.
MANIFEST_APP_PASSWORD=change-me-locally
# Every backing-service credential (§12, D3) is derived from this by HMAC. It must
# be STABLE: a value that changes between control-plane restarts cannot reproduce
# the password an existing database container already holds, and the failure looks
# like a database fault rather than a configuration one.
MANIFEST_MASTER_SECRET=change-me-locally-0000000000000000

# ───────────────────────────────── 2. THE CONTROL PLANE'S SETTINGS ──────────────────────────────────
# The control plane (packages/control-plane) reads its settings from its ENVIRONMENT and checks
# them at boot; packages/control-plane/src/config.ts is the authority, and its comments say why
# each exists. RUNBOOK's "Running the control plane" starts it with `set -a; . ./.env; set +a`
# and then exports the few it requires — so a line you UNCOMMENT here reaches the next control
# plane started that way, and nothing else changes.
#
# WHY EVERY LINE BELOW IS COMMENTED OUT:
#   - The value shown is the BUILT-IN DEFAULT (or, for the required ones, what RUNBOOK's block sets).
#   - `make doctor` requires .env to hold every UNCOMMENTED key in this file, so a new live key here
#     would turn doctor red on every checkout that predates it.
#   - Secrets are never stored twice: the required ones are derived at start from section 1.
#   - Anything uncommented is exported into every shell that sources .env — and the Docker tier's
#     boot tests start control planes with their shell's environment. Run `pnpm test:docker` from a
#     terminal that has not sourced an overridden .env.

# ── 2a. Where applications' code lives — D5's two source drivers ─────────────────────────────────
# ONE driver per control-plane process. Switching is a restart, and a project keeps the driver it
# was created with: on the other driver every source operation on it is refused
# `409 SOURCE_PROVIDER_MISMATCH`. Every demo except `make demo-github` needs driver 1 — and a
# driver-1 demo run against driver 2 CREATES its project there, where no route can delete it.
#   local   bare git repositories under MANIFEST_REPOS_ROOT, on this machine (driver 1)
#   github  a GitHub organisation behind a GitHub App, built from a local mirror kept at the same
#           path (driver 2). With the MANIFEST_GITHUB_* lines left commented, it talks to the
#           GitHub FAKE — `make github-up`, http://127.0.0.1:7110 — whose credentials `make up`
#           mints into infra/secrets/.
# To run against the FAKE: uncomment the next line and change `local` to `github` (then `make
# github-up`, and restart the control plane). To go back: comment it out again, and restart.
# MANIFEST_SOURCE_DRIVER=local
#
# Driver 2's GitHub. The defaults are the FAKE's. Only loopback may be plain http: an installation
# token crosses nothing else unencrypted (CONFIG_GITHUB_INSECURE_URL).
# MANIFEST_GITHUB_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7110/api/v3   # REST API root — GitHub Enterprise Server's layout, which the fake serves
# MANIFEST_GITHUB_GIT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7110          # git over HTTP(S); clone URLs are <this>/<org>/<repo>.git
# MANIFEST_GITHUB_ORG=manifest-apps                       # the organisation every app's repository is created in
# MANIFEST_GITHUB_APP_ID=1000001                          # the GitHub App's numeric id
# MANIFEST_GITHUB_INSTALLATION_ID=2000001                 # that App's installation on the organisation
# MANIFEST_GITHUB_APP_KEY=infra/secrets/github-fake-app.pem           # the App's PRIVATE key: a FILE, mode 600, owner-only (a looser one refuses the boot)
# MANIFEST_GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=infra/secrets/github-fake-webhook.secret  # the webhook HMAC secret: a FILE, the same custody
#
# A REAL GitHub App instead — e.g. `Manifest (local dev)` (the D5 plan's "What Rich does" 2 has
# every setting to register one). Uncomment all of these together. What changes:
#   - it needs the network, and creates a REAL private repository per project, which nothing
#     deletes — remove them on github.com by hand;
#   - GitHub cannot reach a laptop, so there are NO webhooks: the platform learns of a push when it
#     next reads the repository (the console's Re-validate, or a build);
#   - on a FREE organisation GitHub will not protect a private repository's `main`, and the project
#     says so ("main NOT protected", with GitHub's own words);
#   - never reuse a project name across the fake and a real App — both are provider `github`.
# MANIFEST_SOURCE_DRIVER=github
# MANIFEST_GITHUB_API_URL=https://api.github.com
# MANIFEST_GITHUB_GIT_URL=https://github.com
# MANIFEST_GITHUB_ORG=<your organisation — Manifest-local-dev for Manifest (local dev)>
# MANIFEST_GITHUB_APP_ID=<the App's id — 5068172 for Manifest (local dev)>
# MANIFEST_GITHUB_INSTALLATION_ID=<its installation id — 164652178 for Manifest (local dev)>
# MANIFEST_GITHUB_APP_KEY=infra/secrets/github-app.pem
#   (the webhook secret can stay the fake's file: nothing will deliver to a laptop)

# ── 2b. Required — RUNBOOK's block exports these at every start, derived from section 1 ────────────
# MANIFEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://manifest_app:${MANIFEST_APP_PASSWORD}@127.0.0.1:7103/manifest_control   # the control plane's own role — never the superuser (§20)
# MANIFEST_ADMIN_DATABASE_URL=postgres://manifest:${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}@127.0.0.1:7103/manifest_control     # migrations and the test harness ONLY; the control plane never reads it
# MANIFEST_IDP_DATABASE_URL=postgres://manifest:${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}@127.0.0.1:7103/manifest_idp           # the IdP's SP-metadata database — its own setting, never derived from the first
# MANIFEST_SESSION_SECRET=<32 or more random characters — RUNBOOK makes a new one per start, so a restart signs everybody out of the console>
# MANIFEST_BLUEPRINTS_ROOT=$PWD/blueprints
# MANIFEST_REPOS_ROOT=$PWD/.manifest/repos          # driver 1's bare repositories, and driver 2's mirrors, at the same path
# MANIFEST_LITELLM_MASTER_KEY=${LITELLM_MASTER_KEY} # mints and revokes every app's AI key — the SAME secret as section 1's, never a second stored copy

# ── 2c. The environment, and identity (§9, §20) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MANIFEST_ENV=development                          # development | staging | production. Outside development,
#                                                   #   MANIFEST_MASTER_SECRET, MANIFEST_BUILD_CREDENTIAL_SECRET and
#                                                   #   MANIFEST_LITELLM_MASTER_KEY become required
# MANIFEST_PORT=7100                                # the API's port, on 127.0.0.1; the edge proxies to it
# MANIFEST_CONTROL_PLANE_ORIGIN=https://console.manifest.internal   # where people reach the console and the API — the FIRST origin: its ACS is index 0 and its SLO the one SingleLogoutService
# MANIFEST_FRONTEND_ORIGIN=https://app.manifest.internal            # the faculty front-end's origin (§21); EMPTY disables it. A request is judged by the origin it ARRIVED on (its Host):
#                                                   #   a cookie-carrying change must name THAT origin, and each origin signs a person in on itself
# MANIFEST_SP_ENTITY_BASE=https://manifest.internal # every SAML SP entityID is <this>/sp/<slug>/<env>; manifest.ubc.ca at UBC
# MANIFEST_IDP_ENTITY_ID=https://idp.manifest.internal/idp/shibboleth   # the IdP's entityID — UBC's has the same shape
# MANIFEST_IDP_BASE_URL=https://idp.manifest.internal                   # what apps' SAML sign-in and sign-out URLs are built from (sandbox, staging)
# MANIFEST_IDP_SIGNING_CERT=infra/idp/cert/server.crt                   # the IdP's public signing certificate, minted by `make up`
# MANIFEST_SP_PRIVATE_KEY=infra/sp/control-plane.key                    # the control plane's own SP keypair, minted by `make up`
# MANIFEST_SP_CERTIFICATE=infra/sp/control-plane.crt
# MANIFEST_REHEARSAL_USER=instructor                # who D21's pre-launch rehearsal signs in as — UBC's staging IdP changes these two and nothing else
# MANIFEST_REHEARSAL_PASSWORD=instructor

# ── 2d. Zones and the edge (§12, §23) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MANIFEST_ZONE_SANDBOX=sandbox.manifest.internal
# MANIFEST_ZONE_STAGING=staging.manifest.internal
# MANIFEST_ZONE_PRODUCTION=manifest.internal
# MANIFEST_CADDY_ADMIN_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7119    # the edge's admin API, where runtime routes are applied
# MANIFEST_CADDY_SERVER_INTERNAL=srv0               # the internal listener (127.0.0.2): staging, sandbox, the console
# MANIFEST_CADDY_SERVER_PUBLIC=srv1                 # the public listener (127.0.0.3): production only
# MANIFEST_EDGE_PUBLIC_PORT=8443                    # the public listener's port INSIDE the edge container
# MANIFEST_DNS_SERVER=10.89.0.53                    # the containers' resolver, on the platform network
# MANIFEST_CA_CERT=infra/ca/manifest-root.crt       # the platform CA `make seed` mints; readiness probes verify against it

# ── 2e. Builds, the registry and stored secrets (§12, §13, §20) ─────────────────────────────────────
# MANIFEST_REGISTRY_URL=127.0.0.1:7107              # the registry as the host and the daemon reach it
# MANIFEST_REGISTRY_INTERNAL_URL=manifest-registry:5000   # the same registry as a container reaches it — not interchangeable
# MANIFEST_REGISTRY_TOKEN_KEY=infra/registry-auth/token.key   # signs the registry's scoped tokens (`make seed` mints the pair)
# MANIFEST_REGISTRY_TOKEN_CERT=infra/registry-auth/token.crt
# MANIFEST_BUILD_CREDENTIAL_SECRET=<32+ characters — optional in development, required outside it>
# MANIFEST_SECRETS_MASTER_KEY=infra/secrets/master.key     # the envelope-encryption keypair, kept apart from the database it opens
# MANIFEST_DOCKER_SOCKET=<auto-detected — Docker Desktop's socket; set only if yours is elsewhere>
# MANIFEST_RESERVED_LABELS_DIR=infra/reserved-labels       # §23's names no project may take, read at boot

# ── 2f. Deploys and AI (§10, §11) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MANIFEST_READINESS_TIMEOUT_MS=90000               # how long a deploy waits for the app to answer at its hostname
# MANIFEST_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_MS=120000                  # how long a retire lets the old instance finish in-flight requests
# MANIFEST_LITELLM_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7106        # LiteLLM as the control plane reaches it
# MANIFEST_LITELLM_INTERNAL_URL=http://manifest-litellm:4000/v1   # LiteLLM as an APP reaches it (§8's LLM_ENDPOINT) — not interchangeable
# MANIFEST_AI_ENABLED=1                             # '0' only to run without LiteLLM; it never loosens what an app's key may do
# MANIFEST_AGENT_MONTHLY_USD=10                     # a person's monthly budget for agent sessions, on their own LiteLLM user (§10)
# MANIFEST_AGENT_SESSION_CAP_USD=2                  # one agent session's cap — never more than what remains of the person's month
# MANIFEST_AGENT_LLM_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7106/v1   # where an agent (or intake) key is USED — answered to the client, never called here
# MANIFEST_INTAKE_MODEL=default-chat                # the ONE model intake keys call — a catalogue entry D17 allows for `internal`, checked at every mint
# MANIFEST_INTAKE_KEY_CAP_USD=0.25                  # one intake key's cap (the platform pays for intake, §10)
# MANIFEST_INTAKE_KEY_MINUTES=30                    # one intake key's life — never past the signed-in session that asked for it
# MANIFEST_INTAKE_DAILY_KEYS=10                     # intake keys a person may start in a Vancouver day
# MANIFEST_INTAKE_MONTHLY_USD=50                    # the platform's monthly intake budget, on LiteLLM user `mf-platform-intake`
# MANIFEST_CAPABLE_MODEL=openai/gpt-6-luna          # the CAPABLE model: registered at boot as `default-chat-large` at `internal` (§7, §26); unset registers none and removes one; needs the network, and a price LiteLLM knows
# OPENAI_API_KEY=<the provider's key>               # read by LiteLLM ALONE (infra/compose.yaml); the control plane scrubs it at boot and never reads it; `make up` after changing it; a key costs real money

# ── 3. PER-COMMAND SWITCHES — put these on ONE command line, never in this file ──────────────────────
# MANIFEST_ORIGIN=https://console.manifest.internal # where the demos and the journey reach the API (scripts/lib/api.sh)
# MANIFEST_FAKE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7110           # where `make demo-github` and clear_orphan_repository reach the GitHub fake
# MANIFEST_VERIFY_OFFLINE=1                         # `make verify` adds the offline checks (the offline acceptance sets it)
# MANIFEST_CONSOLE_PORT=7104                        # `make demo-console`'s port
# MANIFEST_CONSOLE_PREFLIGHT_ONLY=1                 # `make demo-console` builds, checks the edge serves it, and stops
# MANIFEST_TEST_DOCKER=1                            # `pnpm test:docker` sets it; the Docker tier FAILS rather than skips without it
# MANIFEST_MOCK_PORT=7102                           # manifest-mock's port
# MANIFEST_MOCK_ROLE=admin                          # manifest-mock signs you in as an administrator (the fleet screen)
# MANIFEST_MOCK_FAIL=1                              # manifest-mock plays a deploy that never becomes ready
# MANIFEST_MOCK_SCAN_MS=<milliseconds>              # manifest-mock's pause before a build's scan result
#   Not here at all: LITELLM_DIGEST (read from infra/images.lock by the Makefile — the one place digests
#   live) and the fake's own FAKE_* settings (infra/compose.yaml sets them).
